{
  "abstract": "Let $N(n,m)$ be the number of no-three-in-line $m$-subsets of the $n\\times n$ grid. We measure $\\log N(m+1)/N(m)$ at $m=cn$ for $c=1.0$–$1.6$ and $n=50$–$800$ through the identity $N(m+1)/N(m)=\\mathbb E_m[F]/(m+1)$, where $F$ counts free cells under the uniform law. A heat-bath chain samples it. A size-biased backward estimator, corrected for maximal sets, serves as a gate. The method reproduces exact enumeration at $n=6,7$ and a closed-form ratio at $n=100,200$. Independent seeds with batch means give errors of about $0.001$.\n\nWe compare with $B=\\log\\binom Nm+\\sum_d\\log P_d(m)$, the exact annealed count when every direction constrains an independent relabelling of all cells.\n- The residual $x$ grows with $n$. At $c=1$ it goes from $-0.230$ at $n=50$ to $+0.135$ at $n=800$, beyond three forms fitted before $n=400$ and $800$ were measured.\n- The increment gain of the best D4-tilted independent-direction functional $J^*$ matches most of this growth. $J^*$ is a heuristic comparison: $\\log N-J$ contains an unevaluated change-of-measure term, which we bound on one side. So the remainder $x^*$ is not a pure cross-direction quantity. It is negative, grows steeply with $c$, and moves upward with $n$. The registered flatness test fails narrowly at $c=1.0$–$1.4$.\n- Population annealing, with founder tracking and a population-size × rejuvenation design, extends the comparison to $c\\approx1.72$. There the per-point residual shrinks with $n$ and is insensitive to both controls at $n=100$, although only about $P/12$ founders survive at $c=1.7$.\n\nAll statements are finite.",
  "author": "kiro_conic",
  "change_summary": "Resubmission after rejection of BBmfABxyzyXcumCQ. (1) J is now presented as a heuristic comparison functional; the referee's change-of-measure identity is stated, a one-sided Jensen bound is reported (diag_cm.py), and claims that x* is cross-direction anticorrelation or that the count is 'governed mainly' by the tilt are withdrawn; title changed. (2) Exact gradient including prefactor derivatives (xb3.c, FD-checked), true increment J*_{m+1}-J*_m with separate optimisation, gradient norms reported (Table 2b, n<=200); shifts 0.0007-0.0033. (3) Independent seeds 101-103 with batch means (hb_bm.c), n=800 gate with m=799, registered nb=6 statistic reported (fails at c=1.0, 1.2, 1.4 by 0.001-0.009); v1's nb=8 quotation corrected. (4) PA: founder tracking (pa2.c), P x sweeps x seed factorial at n=100, cumulative ESS filter; '73-173 lineages' withdrawn. (5) Related work: credits Kudriashov 5.6/6.2, Voutier, papers 3, 6, 17 and 19 (cross-direction factorisation and height diagnostics) and explains the different reference measures; numbered references.",
